KG42.register("rules-d391acfedae0fa2650e0f40f",{"id":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R007","paper":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R007","mechanism_id":"M02","name":"Local market coordinator","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"Total and average energy-consumption information may be updated through communication between the aggregator and the customer's ECS. Scope: Distributed non-cooperative energy scheduling game G. Condition: At each iteration of the distributed scheduling algorithm. The aggregator determines the constant penalizing factor alpha >= 1 a priori. Scope: Non-collaborative scheduling with tiered proportional billing. The aggregator may adjust the penalizing factor alpha to control the degree of fairness between heavy and light customers. Scope: Fairness between heavy and light customers under tiered proportional billing.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.local_operator under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Distributed non-cooperative energy scheduling game G. | Fairness between heavy and light customers under tiered proportional billing. | Non-collaborative scheduling with tiered proportional billing.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g02-e13"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"x_i_tot","symbol":"x_{i,Tot}^{t}","meaning":"total energy consumption of customer i at time-slot t, as used in the tiered-billing and average-consumption definitions","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued total energy consumption during time-slot t","unit":null,"indices":["i","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g02-e13"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"theta-alpha","symbol":"\\alpha","meaning":"constant penalizing factor determined a priori by the aggregator; alpha >= 1; used to control fairness between heavy and light customers under tiered proportional billing","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"\\alpha \\ge 1, determined a priori by the aggregator"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g01-E19"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Total and average energy-consumption information may be updated through communication between the aggregator and the customer's ECS. Scope: Distributed non-cooperative energy scheduling game G. Condition: At each iteration of the distributed scheduling algorithm.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The aggregator determines the constant penalizing factor alpha >= 1 a priori. Scope: Non-collaborative scheduling with tiered proportional billing.","expression":"\\alpha \\ge 1","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta-alpha"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The aggregator may adjust the penalizing factor alpha to control the degree of fairness between heavy and light customers. Scope: Fairness between heavy and light customers under tiered proportional billing.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta-alpha"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The average energy consumption of all customers at time-slot t is the sum of all customers' total energy consumption at that time-slot divided by the number of customers.","expression":"x_{Avg}^{t} = \\frac{\\sum_{i'\\in I} x_{i',Tot}^{t}}{|I|}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":["x_i_tot"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g02-e13"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-54c42059a7-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M02-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Energy Scheduling: Non-Collaborative Approach","anchor_text":"⎪⎩ if xti,T ot > xtAvg, a ∀t ∈T , i ∈I (11) fun de where ¯xt−i,T ot = [xti′,T ot]i′̸=i denotes the e","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"where \\bar{x}_{-i,Tot}^t=[x_{i',Tot}^t]_{i'\\ne i} denotes the energy consumptions of all customers except for customer i's energy consumption at time-slot t, x_{Avg}^t=\\sum_{i'\\in I}x_{i',Tot}^t/|I| denotes the average energy consumption of all customers at time-slot t, and \\alpha\\ge1 is a constant penalizing factor which is determined a priori by the aggregator. Each customer is subject to two-tier electricity rates according to its own energy consumption, x_{i,Tot}^t as well as the average energy consumption, x_{Avg}^t, for each time-slot. Specifically, when a customer's energy consumption is less than or equal to the average consumption, i.e., x_{i,Tot}^t\\le x_{Avg}^t, the base rate is applied, which is represented as C^t(\\sum_{i'\\in I}x_{i',Tot}^t)/\\sum_{i'\\in I}x_{i',Tot}^t, and the bill is charged proportionally to the amount of energy consumption. On the other hand, when a customer's energy consumption is larger than the average consumption, i.e., x_{i,Tot}^t>x_{Avg}^t, the base rate is applied to the energy consumption below the average value, x_{Avg}^t, while the penalized rate is applied to the energy consumption beyond the average value, x_{i,Tot}^t-x_{Avg}^t. The penalized rate is obtained by multiplying the base rate by the penalizing factor, \\alpha, i.e., \\alpha C^t(\\sum_{i'\\in I}x_{i',Tot}^t)/\\sum_{i'\\in I}x_{i',Tot}^t."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E19","location":{"location_id":"src-54c42059a7-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M02-settlement","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Energy Scheduling: Non-Collaborative Approach","anchor_text":"other hand, when a customer’s energy consumption is larger fol than the average consumption, i.e., x","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Here, the penalizing factor \\alpha has two meanings. First, as \\alpha increases, heavy customers, who consume more energy than the average consumption, will pay more per unit energy consumption compared to the light customers, who consume less energy than the average consumption. Hence, by adjusting \\alpha, the aggregator can control the degree of fairness between heavy and light customers. Second, \\alpha affects the aggregator's profit. For example, if \\alpha=1, the sum of bills charged to all customers is equal to the total cost that the aggregator has to pay to the utility company, whereas if \\alpha>1, the aggregator can make a profit by charging heavy customers a higher rate."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-54c42059a7-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M02-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":"1223","section":"IV. Energy Scheduling: Non-Collaborative Approach","anchor_text":"er following vector: se ge g(¯x) = [∇¯x1u1(¯x1, ¯x−1); · · · ; ∇¯x|I|u|I|(¯x|I|, ¯x−|I|)] (15) gy an","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the proposed algorithm, each customer updates its own energy scheduling decision and energy trading based on the subgradient \\nabla_{\\bar{x}_i^{(k)}} u_i(\\bar{x}_i^{(k)},\\bar{x}_{-i}^{(k)}) at each iteration k in a distributed manner. Each customer needs to acquire the wholesale price function, p^t(\\cdot), \\forall t\\in T, the total amount of energy consumption, \\sum_{i'\\in I} x_{i',Tot}^{t,(k)}, \\forall t\\in T, and the average energy consumption x_{Avg}^{t,(k)}, \\forall t\\in T at each iteration. The above information can be updated at each iteration through the communication between the aggregator and the customer's ECS."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M02-coordination","v141-a-M02-pricing","v141-a-M02-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","quote":"the total amount of energy consumption, \\sum_{i'\\in I} x_{i',Tot}^{t,(k)}, \\forall t\\in T, and the average energy consumption x_{Avg}^{t,(k)}, \\forall t\\in T at each iteration. The above information can be updated at each iteration through the communication between the aggregator and the customer's ECS."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E18","quote":"\\alpha\\ge1 is a constant penalizing factor which is determined a priori by the aggregator."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E19","quote":"Hence, by adjusting \\alpha, the aggregator can control the degree of fairness between heavy and light customers."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"7dac9ce2f245ecb51a0c5ce6b13e2dba21365d433f81361d405ce4da2c25e40a","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"The rule is a coordination/information-exchange rule. The frozen graph contains only coordination.local_operator with no edges and no typed x/theta. Source evidence supports the alpha >= 1 parameter bound and the average-consumption definition, which are formalized provisionally. However, the core communication relation between the aggregator and each customer's ECS and the per-iteration information acquisition cannot be represented without additional graph objects/edges. B evidence remains unreviewed; no independent source audit is claimed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"x_i_tot","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The local coordinator's per-iteration information exchange concerns the customers' total energy consumption x_{i,Tot}^{t}; the variable is the underlying customer operational quantity whose aggregate and average are communicated."},{"object_id":"theta-alpha","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The aggregator/local coordinator determines the constant penalizing factor alpha a priori (alpha >= 1), which parameterizes the tiered billing coordination."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The constraint records the source-supported bound alpha >= 1 on the penalizing factor set a priori by the local coordinator."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C004","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The average-consumption definition is the mathematical content of the total/average information that the local coordinator updates and communicates to customers each iteration."}],"revision_requests":["Add declared variable x_{i,Tot}^{t} (customer total energy consumption) and parameter alpha (penalizing factor, alpha >= 1) to the frozen graph with bindings to coordination.local_operator; the graph currently has x=[] and theta=[] for this rule.","Add a graph representation of the communication relation between the aggregator and each customer's ECS at each iteration (e.g., participant/message nodes or an edge) because the frozen graph for this rule has only the unary coordination.local_operator and E=[]; source C001 describes a two-party exchange.","Clarify ownership between R007 and R008 of the shared E13 information-acquisition statement and the average-consumption definition; E13 is attached to both rules, but the graph cannot currently distinguish local-operator communication from price-signal acquisition.","If the subgradient update in (14) is intended to be part of this coordination rule, add a clearing/algorithm node and variable objects; it is currently not represented in R007 and should not be moved from M02 clearing."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
